From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slothfulchat <patches@slothfulchat.invalid>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 00:32:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 87/90] web-app: reactions bar inside the message context menu

Reacting took two steps (right-click, "React", then a separate bar) or a
hover icon. Signal and Telegram put the reactions on top of the message
menu; do the same.

ContextMenu gains an optional `header` component, rendered inside the
modal <dialog> (anything outside it is inert while the menu is open) and
positioned with the menu as one block: with room, the menu opens right
at the cursor and the header above it; otherwise the block goes below or
above the cursor, kept on screen on both axes; a
menu taller than the room below the header scrolls. With a header the
menu focuses its first action once on open, so a screen reader announces
the menu; ArrowUp from there reaches the header, the header's roving
tabindex handles left/right, and ArrowDown/ArrowUp from it enter the
menu at its first/last item. Item highlight is :focus-visible, so a
mouse- or touch-opened menu doesn't look pre-selected.

Message passes the ReactionsBar as the header and drops the "React"
item; picking a reaction closes the menu before the RPC (no double
send). "More emojis" closes the menu and hands over to the standalone
bar with the picker open, which already keeps the large picker on
screen. Ctrl/Cmd+R is unchanged. The bar has no slide-in inside the
menu, is smaller with a mouse and stays finger-sized on touch; touch
menu items get 16px text and 44px rows.

The hover react / "..." icons are gone and no column is reserved for
them. "..." stays in the DOM, visually hidden until :focus-visible, so
keyboard and screen-reader users keep a way in (macOS has no Menu key);
Enter on the focused message itself opens the menu as well (not on a
link, media control or clickable info message), listed in the shortcuts
sheet and in aria-keyshortcuts. The saved-messages "show in chat"
button stays.

Keyboard details: Tab closes the menu (APG) and an auto-repeated Enter
is ignored, so holding Enter can't trigger the item it lands on. The
standalone bar returns focus to the message when a pick or Escape closes
it (not when a click or scroll elsewhere hides it), and its positioning helper hides the bar transparently while
measuring (visibility: hidden made the picker's search unfocusable, so
its autofocus was lost when the menu hands over to it).

The layer's dialog dispatches `close` as a separate task; a menu
reopened in between (Escape, then Enter right away) was emptied by the
late handler. onClose now leaves a reopened dialog alone, and a new
open settles the previous menu's promise and remounts the menu, so it
is positioned and focused afresh.

Phones: a long press anywhere on a message opens the menu. On coarse
pointers nothing in a bubble is selectable: iOS otherwise starts its own
text selection ~500ms into the press and cancels the touch, and with it
0079's long-press fallback, so the menu never opened on iPhone. "Copy
Text" copies the message, as in other messengers. Message links get
-webkit-touch-callout: none so iOS's preview sheet doesn't cover the
menu.
